<title>ESTONIA: HANSA HAD 37 PCT OF MAY BOURSE TRADE.</title>
<headline>HANSA HAD 37 PCT OF MAY BOURSE TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading bank Hansapank accounted for 37 percent of turnover on the Tallinn bourse in May, up from 34 percent the previous month, the bourse said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Hoiupank made up 16 percent, while Forekspank and Uhispank both had 10 percent of the total turnover in May, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>Total bourse turnover was 906 million kroons last month.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
